/* Manu Tere · zh · pack rpn · generated by build.py; loaded with the pack */
__mtLangPack('zh','rpn',{"The body and the head":"身体和头部","Carved from the tuff, compressed volcanic ash, of the crater Rano Raraku. Nearly all of the more than {#1} moai come from there, and almost {#2} still stand in and around the quarry.":"用 Rano Raraku 火山口的凝灰岩（压实的火山灰）雕刻而成。{#1} 多座 moai 几乎全部来自那里，还有将近 {#2} 座仍然立在采石场里和周围。","The red topknot, the":"红色石髻，","Red scoria from the small crater Puna Pau, carved separately and raised onto some of the moai.":"用 Puna Pau 小火山口的红色火山渣单独雕刻，再安放到一些 moai 的头上。","White coral, with pupils of black obsidian or red scoria. Set in the sockets, they “opened” the moai.":"白色珊瑚，瞳孔是黑曜石或红色火山渣。把眼睛嵌进眼窝，moai 就“睁开了眼”。","The platform, the":"石台，","Fitted blocks of basalt and beach stones: the ahu is the sacred platform the moai stand on.":"拼合的玄武岩石块和海滩石头：ahu 是安放 moai 的神圣石台。","Rano Raraku: soft volcanic tuff":"Rano Raraku：柔软的火山凝灰岩","Puna Pau: red scoria":"Puna Pau：红色火山渣","White coral and black obsidian":"白色珊瑚和黑曜石","Basalt blocks and beach stones":"玄武岩石块和海滩石头","A moai on its ahu":"立在 ahu 上的一座 moai","<b>{A}. {B}:</b> where does it come from?":"<b>{A}. {B}：</b>它来自哪里？","Not from there. Think about the colour and the stone.":"不是那里。想想它的颜色和石头。","<b>Make the moai walk.</b> Oral tradition says the moai walked to their ahu. Experiments with a replica show that a team with ropes can “walk” a statue upright by rocking it from side to side. <b>Pull left, then right, then left…</b>":"<b>让 moai 走起来。</b>口头传说讲，moai 是自己走到 ahu 上的。用复制品做的实验表明，一队人拉着绳子，让石像左右摇晃，就能让它直立着“走路”。<b>向左拉，再向右拉，再向左拉……</b>","Pull left":"向左拉","Pull right":"向右拉","Same side twice: it rocks too far and could fall! Alternate.":"同一边拉了两次：它晃得太厉害，可能会倒！要左右交替。","It rocks… and steps forward.":"它摇晃着……向前迈了一步。","Another step!":"又一步！","Keep the rhythm.":"保持节奏。","It reaches the ahu!":"它到达 ahu 了！","Your moai stands on its ahu. Visitors arrive at Ahu Tongariki. What is right?":"你的 moai 立在了它的 ahu 上。游客来到 Ahu Tongariki。怎样做才对？","Stay on the path, behind the ropes, with a guide: never touch a moai or step on an ahu":"跟着导游，走在小路上，站在绳子后面：永远不要触摸 moai，也不要踩上 ahu","Yes. Moai are the living faces of ancestors and the ahu are sacred. Touching or climbing them is forbidden and fined.":"对。moai 是祖先活生生的面容，ahu 是神圣的。触摸或攀爬它们是被禁止的，还会被罚款。","A photo touching the moai’s nose":"拍一张摸着 moai 鼻子的照片","Never: touching a moai is forbidden.":"绝对不行：触摸 moai 是被禁止的。","Sit on the ahu to rest":"坐在 ahu 上休息","The ahu is sacred, often a burial place: never step or sit on it.":"ahu 是神圣的，常常也是墓地：永远不要踩或坐在上面。","You know where each part of a moai comes from, you made one walk, and you know how to visit them. Moai face inland, towards the people, watching over them. Most average about {#1} m and {#2} tonnes; the heaviest ever raised, at Ahu Tongariki, weighs about {#3} tonnes.":"你知道了 moai 的每个部分来自哪里，让一座 moai 走了起来，也知道了该怎样参观它们。moai 面朝内陆，朝向人们，守护着他们。大多数平均高约 {#1} m、重约 {#2} 吨；立起来过的最重的一座在 Ahu Tongariki，重约 {#3} 吨。","The cliff of Orongo, the sea and the islet Motu Nui":"Orongo 的悬崖、大海和小岛 Motu Nui","In early July the young men chosen by their chiefs, the <b>hopu manu</b>, gathered at Orongo. Each had to <b>climb down</b> a cliff of about {#1} m. Tap the glowing handholds, one after the other.":"每年七月初，由首领选出的年轻人——<b>hopu manu</b>——聚集在 Orongo。每个人都要<b>爬下</b>一道约 {#1} m 高的悬崖。依次点击发光的抓点。","Careful! Take the next handhold.":"小心！抓住下一个抓点。","Not yet: wait for the birds to lay.":"还没到时候：等鸟儿来下蛋。","Only a stone. Watch where the manutara lands.":"只是一块石头。注意看 manutara 落在哪里。","The first egg!":"第一枚蛋！","You shout your chief’s name to the watchers on the cliff, then tie the egg in a band around your forehead.":"你向悬崖上的守望者喊出你首领的名字，然后用带子把蛋绑在额头上。","Swim back":"游回去","with the egg. Same rule: let the big waves pass.":"，带着蛋。同样的规则：让大浪先过去。","more than a kilometre to Motu Nui on a":"一公里多，到 Motu Nui 去，乘着一个",", a float of totora reeds, through currents and sharks. Hold":"，一种用 totora 芦苇做的浮具，穿过海流，躲开鲨鱼。按住","when a big wave comes, and float over it.":"，从浪上漂过去。","You wait on Motu Nui for days, even weeks, until the <b>manutara</b>, the sooty terns, come to lay. Watch the rocks: <b>tap the first egg</b>.":"你在 Motu Nui 上等了好几天，甚至好几个星期，直到 <b>manutara</b>（乌燕鸥）飞来下蛋。注意看岩石：<b>点击第一枚蛋</b>。","A big wave is coming… let go!":"大浪来了……松开！","The wave rolls you back. Float over the next one!":"大浪把你推了回去。从下一个浪上漂过去！","You floated over it. Swim on!":"你从浪上漂过去了。继续游！","You climbed back to Orongo with the egg unbroken. Your chief became the tangata manu, the birdman, sacred for a year. The race was held each year until the {#1}s; more than {#2} birdman figures are carved in the rocks of Orongo.":"你带着完好无损的蛋爬回了 Orongo。你的首领成了 tangata manu，也就是鸟人，一整年都是神圣的。这项竞赛每年举行，一直持续到 {#1} 年代；Orongo 的岩石上刻着 {#2} 多个鸟人图案。","A manutara has laid! Where?":"一只 manutara 下蛋了！在哪里？","A wooden rongorongo tablet":"一块 rongorongo 木板","About {#1} wooden tablets with <span>rongorongo</span> survive, all in museums far from the island; no one can read them today. But we know <b>how</b> they were read: start at the <b>bottom left</b>, read the line <b>left to right</b>, then <b>turn the tablet upside down</b> for the next line. Every other line is upside down: this is called reverse boustrophedon.":"大约有 {#1} 块刻着 <span>rongorongo</span> 的木板保存了下来，全都在远离小岛的博物馆里；如今没有人能读懂它们。但我们知道它们是<b>怎样</b>读的：从<b>左下角</b>开始，<b>从左到右</b>读一行，然后<b>把木板倒转过来</b>读下一行。每隔一行都是倒着的：这叫作反向牛耕式。","The shapes here are simple drawings inspired by the glyphs (birds, people, fish, plants), not copies of real signs.":"这里的图形是受这些符号启发画的简单图画（鸟、人、鱼、植物），并不是真实符号的复制品。","Turn the tablet first: the next line is upside down.":"先把木板转过来：下一行是倒着的。","You have already read that line.":"这一行你已经读过了。","Start at the bottom left.":"从左下角开始。","Read the next line: it is upright now, just below the one you read.":"读下一行：它现在是正的，就在你刚读的那一行下面。","Left to right, one sign after the other.":"从左到右，一个符号接一个符号。","The whole tablet, read the old way!":"整块木板，用古老的方式读完了！","You read a tablet the rongorongo way: bottom left, left to right, turning it at every line. In Rapa Nui, rongorongo means to recite or chant. The script is still undeciphered; tradition says it was carved with obsidian flakes and shark teeth.":"你用 rongorongo 的方式读了一块木板：从左下角开始，从左到右，每读完一行就转一次木板。在 Rapa Nui 语里，rongorongo 的意思是背诵或吟唱。这种文字至今仍未被破译；传说它是用黑曜石薄片和鲨鱼牙齿刻出来的。","End of the line. Now turn the tablet.":"这一行读完了。现在把木板转过来。","Turn the tablet":"转动木板","The line you just read is now at the top, upside down. The next line is upright just below it: read it from the left.":"你刚读的那一行现在在最上面，是倒着的。下一行就在它下面，是正的：从左边开始读。","Sliding down the grassy slope of Maunga Puʻi on banana trunks":"骑着香蕉树干从 Maunga Puʻi 的草坡上滑下来","At the <b>Tapati Rapa Nui</b> festival in February, riders lie on two banana trunks tied together and slide down Maunga Puʻi: about {#1} m of grass, at up to {#2} or {#3} km/h, in about {#4} seconds. No brakes and no steering: <b>keep your balance</b> with Left and Right.":"在二月的 <b>Tapati Rapa Nui</b> 节上，选手躺在绑在一起的两根香蕉树干上，从 Maunga Puʻi 上滑下来：约 {#1} m 的草坡，时速最高可达 {#2} 到 {#3} km/h，大约 {#4} 秒就到底。没有刹车，也没法转向：用左和右<b>保持平衡</b>。","Ready on the hilltop…":"在山顶准备好……","Haka pei!":"Haka pei!","Thrown off into the grass! Walk back up and try again.":"被甩进草丛里了！走回山顶再试一次。","At the bottom, still on your trunks!":"到底了，还稳稳地在树干上！","(after {A} tries)":"（试了 {A} 次）","You slid all the way down Maunga Puʻi{A}. Haka pei is thought to come from an old rite of passage or warrior training; it was revived and is now one of the highlights of Tapati, with races, body painting (takona) and canoe events.":"你从 Maunga Puʻi 一路滑到了底{A}。人们认为 haka pei 源自古老的成年礼或武士训练；后来它被重新恢复，如今是 Tapati 节的亮点之一，还有赛跑、人体彩绘（takona）和独木舟比赛。","Planting a toromiro in a stone circle":"在石圈里种一棵 toromiro","The <span>toromiro</span> is Rapa Nui’s own tree: dense red wood once carved into figures, and clusters of bright yellow flowers. The last wild tree grew in the crater of Rano Kau and was gone by {#1}. Its seeds survived in botanical gardens far away, and are now coming home. <b>{#2}. Build a manavai:</b> a ring of volcanic stones that shelters young plants from the wind and keeps the soil moist. Tap each spot.":"<span>toromiro</span> 是 Rapa Nui 独有的树：木材致密发红，从前被雕成人像，还会开出一簇簇鲜黄色的花。最后一棵野生的树长在 Rano Kau 火山口里，到 {#1} 年已经消失了。它的种子在遥远的植物园里保存了下来，现在正回到家乡。<b>{#2}. 建一个 manavai：</b>一圈火山石，为幼苗挡风，让土壤保持湿润。点击每个位置。","<b>{#1}. Prepare the soil.</b> The toromiro is a legume, like peas and beans. What does its root need?":"<b>{#1}. 准备土壤。</b>toromiro 是豆科植物，和豌豆、豆子一样。它的根需要什么？","Tiny root bacteria, rhizobia, that help it feed on nitrogen from the air":"根上的微小细菌——根瘤菌，帮助它利用空气中的氮","A little sea water, for the minerals":"一点海水，补充矿物质","Nothing: it grew here alone before":"什么都不要：它以前就是自己在这里长大的","Salt water would harm the roots.":"盐水会伤害根。","Its old partner bacteria may have vanished with the last trees: replantings in the {#1}s failed. It needs help.":"它原来的伙伴细菌可能随着最后的那些树一起消失了：{#1} 年代的重新种植都失败了。它需要帮助。","Yes. Researchers are looking for root bacteria from neighbouring islands that suit the toromiro.":"对。研究人员正在附近的岛上寻找适合 toromiro 的根部细菌。","<b>{#1}. Plant and water.</b> The young toromiro sits in the centre of the manavai. <b>Hold</b> to water it, and stop in the green zone: not too little, not too much.":"<b>{#1}. 种下并浇水。</b>小 toromiro 种在 manavai 的中央。<b>按住</b>来浇水，在绿色区域停下：不能太少，也不能太多。","Hold to water":"按住浇水","Still dry: a little more.":"还是干的：再多一点。","Too much: the roots would rot. Let it drain…":"太多了：根会烂掉。让水渗下去……","Just right.":"刚刚好。","Seasons pass inside the stone circle…":"石圈里，四季流转……","Your toromiro flowers yellow inside its manavai. On Rapa Nui, the forestry service CONAF grows native plants in its Mataveri Otai nursery and builds stone circles to shelter them, with help from botanic gardens abroad.":"你的 toromiro 在 manavai 里开出了黄色的花。在 Rapa Nui，林业部门 CONAF 在 Mataveri Otai 苗圃培育本地植物，并建造石圈为它们挡风，还得到了国外植物园的帮助。","Now <b>swim</b> more than a kilometre to Motu Nui on a <b>pora</b>, a float of totora reeds, through currents and sharks. Hold <b>Swim</b>, but <b>let go</b> when a big wave comes, and float over it.":"现在乘着一个 <b>pora</b>（一种用 totora 芦苇做的浮具）<b>游</b>一公里多，穿过海流，躲开鲨鱼，到 Motu Nui 去。按住<b>游泳</b>，但大浪来时要<b>松开</b>，从浪上漂过去。","<b>The first egg!</b> You shout your chief’s name to the watchers on the cliff, then tie the egg in a band around your forehead.":"<b>第一枚蛋！</b>你向悬崖上的守望者喊出你首领的名字，然后用带子把蛋绑在额头上。","<b>Swim back</b> with the egg. Same rule: let the big waves pass.":"<b>游回去</b>，带着蛋。同样的规则：让大浪先过去。","<b>Climb back up</b> to Orongo with the egg tied to your forehead: tap the handholds in order.":"<b>爬回</b> Orongo，蛋绑在你的额头上：按顺序点击抓手。","<b>Make the moai walk.</b> Oral tradition says the moai walked to their ahu, and experiments show how: three teams with ropes, one on each side and one behind, rock the statue from side to side so that it steps forward. <b>Pull left, then right, then left…</b>":"<b>让 moai 走起来。</b>口头传说讲，moai 是自己走到 ahu 上的，实验也展示了方法：三队人拉着绳子，两边各一队，后面一队，让石像左右摇晃，它就会向前迈步。<b>向左拉，再向右拉，再向左拉……</b>","<b>Open its eyes.</b> On the ahu, eyes of white coral with pupils of obsidian were set into the sockets: only then did the moai come alive, its <b>mana</b> turned on the village. <b>Tap each socket.</b>":"<b>让它睁开眼睛。</b>在 ahu 上，人们把白珊瑚做的眼睛、黑曜石做的瞳孔嵌进眼窝：只有这时 moai 才活了过来，把它的 <b>mana</b> 投向村庄。<b>点击每个眼窝。</b>","<b>Swim back</b> with the egg. Same rule: let the big waves pass, and hold your breath when a shark comes by.":"带着蛋<b>游回去</b>。同样的规则：让大浪先过去，鲨鱼经过时屏住呼吸。","<b>{#1}. Plant and water.</b> The seedling, {#2} cm high, goes into the centre of the manavai. <b>Hold</b> to water it, and stop in the green zone: not too little, not too much.":"<b>{#1}. 种下并浇水。</b>把 {#2} cm 高的幼苗种在 manavai 的中央。<b>按住</b>浇水，在绿色区域停下：不要太少，也不要太多。","<b>{#1}. Read it the old way.</b> About {#2} tablets survive, all in museums far away; no one can read them today. But we know <b>how</b>: start at the <b>bottom left</b>, read the line <b>left to right</b>, then <b>turn the tablet upside down</b> for the next line. Reading was chanting, by the <b>tangata rongorongo</b>.":"<b>{#1}. 用古老的方式读它。</b>大约有 {#2} 块木板保存了下来，全都在远方的博物馆里；如今没有人能读懂它们。但我们知道<b>怎样</b>读：从<b>左下角</b>开始，<b>从左到右</b>读一行，然后<b>把木板倒转过来</b>读下一行。读就是吟唱，由 <b>tangata rongorongo</b> 来念。","A clean, deep line: the glyph is cut.":"一道干净的深线：符号刻好了。","A manutara has laid and flown off! Where?":"一只 manutara 下了蛋飞走了！在哪里？","A rongorongo tablet of dark wood, an irregular board with fluted lines of small glyphs: birdmen, frigatebirds, fish, turtles and plants":"一块深色木头的 rongorongo 木板，形状不规则，板上一行行的槽里刻着小小的符号：鸟人、军舰鸟、鱼、海龟和植物","A tuft of grass! You bounce.":"一丛草！你被颠了起来。","All round. Only the keel along its back holds it now.":"一圈都刻完了。现在只剩背上的岩脊还托着它。","At <b>Rano Raraku</b>, the carvers outlined a moai on the slope of soft tuff and cut a passage around it with basalt picks, <b>toki</b>, working the face first while the statue lay on its back. <b>Tap each glowing point</b> to cut round it, then <b>cut the keel</b> that still holds its back to the rock.":"在 <b>Rano Raraku</b>，雕刻者先在柔软的凝灰岩坡上勾出一座 moai 的轮廓，再用玄武岩镐 <b>toki</b> 在它四周凿出一条通道，石像仰面躺着，先雕脸部。<b>点击每个发光点</b>，绕着它凿一圈，然后<b>凿断岩脊</b>，它的背还靠这道岩脊连在岩石上。","At the <b>Tapati Rapa Nui</b> festival in February, riders painted with <b>takona</b> lie feet first on two banana trunks tied together and slide down <b>Maunga Puʻi</b>: about {#1} m of grass at up to {#2}°, at {#3} or {#4} km/h, in ten seconds. No brakes, no steering. <b>Tap Push</b> to launch, then <b>keep your balance</b> with Left and Right, and steer away from the tufts. The farther you slide on the flat, the better.":"在二月的 <b>Tapati Rapa Nui</b> 节上，画着 <b>takona</b> 彩绘的选手脚朝前躺在绑在一起的两根香蕉树干上，从 <b>Maunga Puʻi</b> 上滑下来：约 {#1} m 的草坡，坡度最高 {#2}°，时速 {#3} 到 {#4} km/h，十秒钟就到底。没有刹车，也没法转向。<b>点击“推”</b>出发，然后用左和右<b>保持平衡</b>，避开草丛。在平地上滑得越远越好。","Back on the hilltop. Push!":"回到山顶。推！","Carved from the tuff, compressed volcanic ash, of the crater Rano Raraku, with basalt picks called toki. About {#1} moai are still in and around the quarry.":"用 Rano Raraku 火山口的凝灰岩（压实的火山灰）雕刻而成，工具是叫作 toki 的玄武岩镐。大约 {#1} 座 moai 仍然留在采石场里和周围。","Chips of tuff fly.":"凝灰岩的碎屑四处飞溅。","Climb to the top of the islet.":"爬到小岛的顶上。","Fitted blocks of basalt and rounded beach stones: the sacred platform the moai stand on, often over burials.":"拼合的玄武岩石块和圆滑的海滩石头：moai 立在上面的神圣石台，下面常常是墓葬。","Free! Now it must be raised, and finished.":"脱离岩石了！现在要把它立起来，再完工。","Hold: obsidian":"按住：黑曜石","Hold: shark tooth":"按住：鲨鱼牙","In spring the <b>hopu manu</b> chosen by their chiefs gathered at <b>Orongo</b>, the village of slab houses on the rim of Rano Kau, among rocks carved with hundreds of birdmen. Each had to <b>climb down</b> the cliff to the sea. Tap the glowing handholds, one after the other.":"春天，由首领选出的 <b>hopu manu</b> 聚集在 <b>Orongo</b>，这座石板屋村庄坐落在 Rano Kau 火山口的边缘，周围的岩石上刻着数百个鸟人。每个人都要<b>爬下</b>悬崖到海边。依次点击发光的抓手。","Its eyes are open: the moai watches over the people.":"它睁开了眼睛：moai 守护着人们。","Its old partner bacteria may have vanished with the last trees: the replantings of the {#1}s failed. It needs help.":"它古老的共生细菌可能随着最后几棵树一起消失了：{#1}年代的重新种植失败了。它需要帮助。","JURY":"评审","Keep the rhythm, the ropes sing.":"保持节奏，绳子在歌唱。","Lay the stones in a ring, one after the other.":"把石头一块接一块地摆成一圈。","Not yet: wait for the manutara to land and lay.":"还没到时候：等 manutara 落下来下蛋。","Now <b>swim</b> more than a kilometre to Motu Nui on a <b>pora</b>, a bundle of totora reeds that carries your food, through currents and sharks. Hold <b>Swim</b>, but <b>let go</b> when a big wave comes, and float over it.":"现在<b>游</b>一公里多到 Motu Nui 去，乘着一个 <b>pora</b>——一捆载着你食物的托托拉芦苇——穿过海流，躲开鲨鱼。按住<b>游泳</b>，但大浪来时要<b>松开</b>，从浪上漂过去。","On the flat! Hold still and slide…":"到平地了！保持不动，滑……","On the hilltop, the team ready to push…":"在山顶上，队伍准备好推了……","Only a stone. Watch where the manutara landed.":"只是一块石头。注意看 manutara 落在了哪里。","Orongo on the rim of the crater Rano Kau: low houses of stone slabs, rocks carved with birdmen, and far below the sea with the three islets of Motu Nui, Motu Iti and the needle of Motu Kao Kao":"Rano Kau 火山口边缘的 Orongo：低矮的石板屋，刻着鸟人的岩石，远远的下方是大海和三座小岛——Motu Nui、Motu Iti 和针尖般的 Motu Kao Kao","Push!":"推！","Red scoria from the small crater Puna Pau, carved separately and raised onto some of the later moai.":"来自 Puna Pau 小火山口的红色火山渣，单独雕刻，再抬到一些较晚的 moai 头上。","Round the head, round the shoulder…":"绕过头部，绕过肩膀……","Scratch the whole outline with the obsidian first.":"先用黑曜石划出整个轮廓。","Seasons pass inside the stone circle: leaves, then the first yellow flowers, then the long pods.":"石圈里季节流转：先是叶子，然后是第一批黄花，再是长长的豆荚。","Shout your chief’s name!":"喊出你首领的名字！","The <span>toromiro</span> is Rapa Nui’s own tree: dense red wood once carved into figures, pinnate leaves and clusters of yellow pea flowers. It grew here before the moai. The last wild one, in the crater of Rano Kau, was gone by {#1}; seeds survived in gardens far away, and at the <b>Mataveri Otai</b> nursery CONAF brings them home. <b>{#2}. Build a manavai:</b> a ring of stacked volcanic stones that shelters the young plant from wind and keeps the soil moist. Tap the glowing spot, round the ring.":"<span>toromiro</span> 是 Rapa Nui 独有的树：致密的红色木材曾被雕成人像，羽状的叶子，一簇簇黄色的豆花。它在 moai 之前就生长在这里。最后一棵野生的长在 Rano Kau 火山口里，到 {#1} 年已经消失；种子在远方的植物园里保存了下来，CONAF 在 <b>Mataveri Otai</b> 苗圃把它们带回家。<b>{#2}. 建一个 manavai：</b>用火山石垒成一圈，为幼苗挡风，让土壤保持湿润。点击发光点，绕圈摆放。","The CONAF nursery of Mataveri Otai under its shade cloth, Rano Kau behind, and a manavai of stacked stones being built for a young toromiro":"遮阳网下的 CONAF Mataveri Otai 苗圃，后面是 Rano Kau，一个用石头垒起的 manavai 正在为一株年幼的 toromiro 建造","The grassy cone of Maunga Puʻi at the Tapati festival: a rider painted with takona lies feet first on two banana trunks at the top; the crowd and the jury wait on the flat below":"Tapati 节上 Maunga Puʻi 的草坡锥形山：山顶上，一名画着 takona 彩绘的选手脚朝前躺在两根香蕉树干上；人群和评审在下方的平地上等待","The passage deepens.":"通道越来越深。","The quarry of Rano Raraku: moai buried to the shoulders on the grassy slope, and one still lying in the rock face":"Rano Raraku 采石场：草坡上埋到肩膀的 moai，还有一座仍然躺在岩壁里","The tablets are driftwood or <i>Thespesia</i> wood, cut in flutes {#1} cm apart with glyphs {#2} cm high. <b>{#3}. Carve a glyph.</b> First <b>hold the obsidian flake</b> to scratch the outline, then <b>hold the shark tooth</b> to deepen it.":"木板是浮木或 <i>Thespesia</i> 木，刻着相距 {#1} cm 的槽，符号高 {#2} cm。<b>{#3}. 刻一个符号。</b>先<b>按住黑曜石薄片</b>划出轮廓，再<b>按住鲨鱼牙</b>把它刻深。","The whole tablet, chanted the old way!":"整块木板，用古老的方式吟唱完了！","Two courses of stone: the manavai is built.":"两层石头：manavai 建好了。","White coral, with pupils of black obsidian or red scoria. Set into the sockets on the ahu, they “opened” the moai.":"白色珊瑚，瞳孔是黑曜石或红色火山渣。在 ahu 上把眼睛嵌进眼窝，moai 就“睁开了眼”。","You climbed down the cliff of Orongo, swam to Motu Nui among the waves and the sharks, found the first egg of the manutara, shouted your chief’s name and brought the egg back unbroken. The race for the god Makemake was held each spring until the {#1}s; more than {#2} birdmen are carved in the rocks of Mata Ngarau at Orongo.":"你爬下了 Orongo 的悬崖，在海浪和鲨鱼之间游到了 Motu Nui，找到了 manutara 的第一枚蛋，喊出了你首领的名字，并把蛋完好无损地带了回来。这场献给 Makemake 神的竞赛每年春天举行，一直持续到 {#1} 年代；Orongo 的 Mata Ngarau 岩石上刻着 {#2} 多个鸟人。","You cut a glyph with obsidian and shark tooth, and read a tablet the rongorongo way: bottom left, left to right, turning it at every line. In Rapa Nui, rongorongo means to recite or chant. About {#1} texts survive, none on the island, and the script is still undeciphered.":"你用黑曜石和鲨鱼牙刻了一个符号，又用 rongorongo 的方式读了一块木板：从左下角开始，从左到右，每读一行就把板子转一圈。在 Rapa Nui 语里，rongorongo 的意思是背诵或吟唱。大约有 {#1} 篇文本保存了下来，岛上一篇也没有，这种文字至今仍未被破译。","You cut a moai from the rock of Rano Raraku, named the stone of each part, walked it to its ahu with three rope teams and opened its eyes. Moai face inland, towards the people, watching over them. Most are about {#1} m and {#2} tonnes; the heaviest ever raised, at Ahu Tongariki, weighs about {#3} tonnes.":"你从 Rano Raraku 的岩石中凿出了一座 moai，说出了每个部分的石材，用三支拉绳队让它走到了它的 ahu 上，还让它睁开了眼睛。moai 面朝内陆，朝向人们，守护着他们。大多数高约 {#1} m、重约 {#2} 吨；立起来过的最重的一座在 Ahu Tongariki，重约 {#3} 吨。","You have already chanted that line.":"这一行你已经唱过了。","You wait on <b>Motu Nui</b> for days, even weeks, sheltering in a cave, until the <b>manutara</b>, the sooty terns, come to lay. Watch the rocks: when a tern lands and leaves, <b>tap the first egg</b>.":"你在 <b>Motu Nui</b> 上等了好几天，甚至好几个星期，躲在洞穴里，直到 <b>manutara</b>（乌燕鸥）飞来下蛋。注意看岩石：当一只燕鸥落下又飞走时，<b>点击第一枚蛋</b>。","Your chief is the <b>tangata manu</b>: his head shaved and painted red and white, he will live apart for a year, sacred, and his clan has the eggs of Motu Nui for the season.":"你的首领成了 <b>tangata manu</b>：他剃光了头，涂上红白两色，将独自隐居一年，是神圣的，而他的部族在这一季拥有 Motu Nui 的鸟蛋。","Your toromiro flowers yellow inside its manavai, and its pods hang ready for new seeds. On Rapa Nui, CONAF grows native plants in its Mataveri Otai nursery and builds stone circles to shelter them, with seeds kept for sixty years by botanic gardens abroad: a tree that was on the island before the moai, coming home.":"你的 toromiro 在它的 manavai 里开出了黄花，豆荚垂下来，准备结出新的种子。在 Rapa Nui，CONAF 在 Mataveri Otai 苗圃培育本土植物，并修建石圈来保护它们，用的是国外植物园保存了六十年的种子：一棵在 moai 之前就生长在岛上的树，正在回家。","coral and obsidian":"珊瑚和黑曜石","the keel":"岩脊","You shout your chief’s name and <b>Ka varu te puoko</b>, “shave your head”: the watchers on the cliff relay it up to Orongo. You tie the egg in a reed band on your forehead and fast for a day. Then you swim back.":"你喊出你首领的名字和 <b>Ka varu te puoko</b>——“剃光你的头”：悬崖上的守望者把它传上 Orongo。你用芦苇带把蛋绑在额头上，禁食一天。然后你游回去。","Push… {#1} / {#2}":"推…… {#1} / {#2}","You stop in front of the jury: {#1} m from the foot of the hill!":"你停在了评审面前：离山脚 {#1} m！"});
